package cve

// cveFTPRDP deepens coverage of two remote-access services attackers probe
// constantly: FTP servers (ProFTPD / vsftpd / Pure-FTPd) and Windows Remote
// Desktop (RDP, RD Gateway, RD Licensing, RD client). FTP command-based exploits
// (mod_copy SITE CPFR/CPTO, wu-ftpd SITE EXEC, the TELNET-IAC overflow) are
// already caught from the control-channel transcript; these add the memory-
// corruption / config / DoS daemon bugs and the RDP-stack RCEs, which are binary
// / client-side and so advisory-only — they drive the fake-vulnerable banner /
// patch-level advertising via ForService. Sources: ProFTPD/vsftpd/Pure-FTPd
// advisories and the Microsoft Security Update Guide. Detection + ATT&CK tagging
// only; nothing is executed.
